From ca9fefa00ff6e056af5a0a76304820e0a18cdf22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 21:30:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] audioserver: delay startup from class core to class main
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

QPR2's more aggressive watchdog kills system_server when audio HAL
initialization takes too long. On some devices (OnePlus/Oppo with QTI
audio HAL), vendor_wifidisplayhalservice_qti triggers lazy IModule/default
lookup before system services have settled, causing the audio HAL to
register and receive binder calls while still parsing its primary
configuration. The null config dereferences at offset 0x18 in a binder
thread, crashing the HAL → audioserver death → system_server stuck in
StartAudioService → watchdog reboot.

Moving audioserver from class core to class main delays its first
connection by several seconds, giving the vendor HAL time to fully
initialize before any binder calls arrive. Audio still initialises
during boot, just later in the sequence.

Issue: #44
---
 media/audioserver/audioserver.rc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/media/audioserver/audioserver.rc b/media/audioserver/audioserver.rc
index 0a8efbd..19052c9 100644
--- a/media/audioserver/audioserver.rc
+++ b/media/audioserver/audioserver.rc
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 service audioserver /system/bin/audioserver
-    class core
+    class main
     user audioserver
     # media gid needed for /dev/fm (radio) and for /data/misc/media (tee)
     group audio camera drmrpc media mediadrm net_bt net_bt_admin net_bw_acct wakelock
-- 
